# React Components

## Patterns in use

- Function components only; default export for App Router pages/layouts
- Never type props inline — declare a named `type` with the `PropsType` naming pattern (e.g. `RootLayoutPropsType`)
- App Router: `src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/app/page.tsx`, Route Handlers under `src/app/api/`
- `lang="pt-br"` on root layout

```tsx
// ✅ Named props type with the PropsType suffix
type RootLayoutPropsType = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
};

export default function RootLayout({ children }: RootLayoutPropsType) {
  return (
    <html lang="pt-br">
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Styling & state

- No CSS framework, CSS Modules, or Tailwind configured yet — keep styles minimal unless the user asks
- No client state library (no Zustand/Redux/Context stores); no TanStack Query yet
- Prefer Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when interactivity requires it

## API routes (Route Handlers)

- Thin handlers: parse request → call service → `NextResponse.json` / status codes
- Always wrap in `try/catch` and use `handleApiError` from `core/errors/handle-api-errors`
- Typed dynamic params via `RouteContext<"/api/...">` when applicable
